        "description": {
         "runs": [
          {
           "text": "In this Huberman Lab Essentials episode, my guest is Dr. Matthew MacDougall, a neurosurgeon at Neuralink. We discuss how brain-machine interfaces could help people with paralysis control computers using their intended movements, and how robotic surgery enables the placement of tiny electrodes in the brain. We also explore advances in brain tumor surgery, implant safety, how the brain and software learn to work together, and the role of animal research. Dr. MacDougall shares his vision for future applications, including restoring movement, addressing mental health conditions and expanding human cognition and communication.\n\nShow notes: "
          },
          {
           "text": "https://www.hubermanlab.com/episode/e...",
           "navigationEndpoint": {
            "urlEndpoint": {
